CAT = "cpafarLiabilities"; SEG = "LIA"
Q = [
("When a company installs an offshore platform it must remove later, the asset retirement obligation is recorded at:",
 "Fair value, added to the asset's cost", ["Undiscounted cost, expensed at once", "Fair value, expensed at once", "Nothing until removal begins"],
 "ASC 410 records the obligation at fair value, usually an expected present value, when incurred, and adds the same amount to the asset's carrying amount, which is then depreciated."),
("An asset retirement obligation is carried at $200,000 and was measured using a 6% credit-adjusted risk-free rate. Accretion for the next year is:",
 "$12,000", ["$0", "$6,000", "$20,000"],
 "Accretion = $200,000 x 6% = $12,000, recorded as accretion expense in operating expenses, not as interest expense."),
("Forty employees have each earned 5 unused vacation days that vest, at $240 a day. The accrued vacation liability is:",
 "$48,000", ["$24,000", "$9,600", "$0"],
 "Vested compensated absences that are probable and estimable are accrued: 40 x 5 x $240 = $48,000."),
("A manager's bonus is 10% of income after the bonus but before taxes. Income before the bonus and taxes is $330,000. The bonus is:",
 "$30,000", ["$33,000", "$27,000", "$36,300"],
 "B = 10% x ($330,000 - B), so 1.1B = $33,000 and B = $30,000. Taking 10% of income before the bonus gives $33,000."),
("A liability for a cash dividend is recorded on the:",
 "Declaration date", ["Date of record", "Payment date", "Ex-dividend date"],
 "Declaration creates a legal obligation, so dividends payable is recorded then. Nothing is recorded on the record date, and payment settles the liability."),
("Employees who are let go receive one-time termination benefits only if they work until the plant closes, beyond the minimum retention period. The cost is recognized:",
 "Ratably over the service period", ["In full on the day it is announced", "When the board approves the plan", "Only when the benefits are paid"],
 "Under ASC 420, when employees must render future service beyond the minimum retention period, the liability is measured at the communication date and recognized ratably over that future service."),
("A self-insured company should accrue a liability for:",
 "Claims incurred, reported or not", ["Expected losses for next year", "Any possible future accident", "Nothing until claims are paid"],
 "A liability exists only for events that have occurred, including incurred but not reported claims. Future accidents have not happened, so no liability exists for them."),
("Five-year bonds with a $500,000 face value and a 6% annual coupon are issued for $460,073 to yield 8%. Interest expense for the first year under the effective interest method is:",
 "$36,806", ["$30,000", "$40,000", "$27,604"],
 "Interest expense = carrying amount x market rate = $460,073 x 8% = $36,806. The $30,000 coupon is the cash paid; the $6,806 difference amortizes the discount."),
("Under current U.S. GAAP, debt issuance costs for a term loan are presented as:",
 "A deduction from the debt", ["A deferred charge asset", "An expense when paid", "A reduction of equity"],
 "ASU 2015-03 presents debt issuance costs as a direct deduction from the carrying amount of the debt, amortized to interest expense over the term."),
("For bonds issued at a premium, interest expense under the effective interest method each period:",
 "Decreases over the term", ["Increases over the term", "Equals the cash coupon", "Stays the same each period"],
 "Premium amortization lowers the carrying amount each period, so carrying amount times the market rate gives a smaller expense each year."),
("Bonds with a $200,000 face value and a $196,000 carrying amount are retired at 101. The company records:",
 "A $6,000 loss", ["A $2,000 loss", "A $4,000 gain", "A $6,000 gain"],
 "The reacquisition price is $202,000. Paying $202,000 to settle a $196,000 liability is a $6,000 loss on extinguishment."),
("When the terms of a borrower's debt are changed, the change is accounted for as an extinguishment if:",
 "Cash flows differ by at least 10%", ["The interest rate is cut at all", "The creditor grants any concession", "The maturity moves by one month"],
 "Under ASC 470-50, new terms are substantially different, and treated as an extinguishment, when the present value of cash flows under them differs by at least 10% from the old."),
("For the borrower, a debt modification is a troubled debt restructuring when:",
 "A struggling debtor gets a concession", ["Both sides agree to any rate cut", "Debt is refinanced at market rates", "Bonds convert under the indenture"],
 "ASC 470-60 applies when the creditor grants a concession it would not otherwise grant because the debtor is in financial difficulty."),
("In a troubled debt restructuring, a debtor's loan has a carrying amount of $210,000. Total undiscounted payments under the new terms are $180,000. The debtor records:",
 "A $30,000 gain", ["No gain; a new rate is imputed", "A $30,000 loss", "A gain at present value"],
 "When future undiscounted payments are less than the carrying amount, the debtor writes the debt down to those payments and recognizes a $30,000 gain. No interest expense is recognized afterwards."),
("A loan covenant caps debt to equity at 2.0. Total liabilities are $1,800,000 and equity is $850,000. The company is:",
 "Not in compliance, at 2.12", ["In compliance, at 1.89", "In compliance, at 0.47", "Not in compliance, at 3.12"],
 "Debt to equity = $1,800,000 / $850,000 = 2.12, above the 2.0 limit, so the covenant is breached."),
("A covenant breach at year-end makes a long-term loan callable by the lender. The loan is classified as:",
 "Current, unless waived for over a year", ["Noncurrent, by its stated maturity", "Disclosed only, not reclassified", "Reclassified into equity"],
 "Debt callable because of a violation is current unless the lender waives its right to demand repayment for more than a year from the balance sheet date, or a grace period cure is probable."),
("Using the cost method, a company buys 1,000 of its shares at $40 and later reissues 600 of them at $45. The reissue credits:",
 "$3,000 to paid-in capital", ["$3,000 to a gain in income", "$3,000 to retained earnings", "$27,000 to common stock"],
 "Treasury stock of $24,000 (600 x $40) is removed and the $3,000 excess goes to paid-in capital from treasury stock. A company never reports gains on its own shares."),
("With 50,000 shares of $1 par stock outstanding at a $30 market price, a company declares a 10% stock dividend. Retained earnings decrease by:",
 "$150,000", ["$5,000", "$0", "$145,000"],
 "A small stock dividend is recorded at fair value: 5,000 shares x $30 = $150,000, with $5,000 to common stock and $145,000 to paid-in capital."),
("A 2-for-1 stock split affects total stockholders' equity by:",
 "No change", ["Doubling it", "Halving it", "Cutting retained earnings"],
 "A split doubles the shares and halves the par value per share. No account balances change, so total equity is the same."),
("A company issues 10,000 shares of $5 par stock at $18 a share and pays $6,000 of issue costs. Additional paid-in capital increases by:",
 "$124,000", ["$130,000", "$180,000", "$174,000"],
 "Proceeds over par are $180,000 - $50,000 = $130,000, and issue costs reduce paid-in capital: $130,000 - $6,000 = $124,000."),
]
